<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Principality of Dombes</h1><p class="st-meta">1523 CE – 1762 CE · capital Trévoux</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small sovereign principality north of Lyon, with its own parliament and mint at Trévoux, held by royal relatives until it was sold to Louis XV.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Dombes, a plateau of ponds east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saone">Saône</a>, belonged to the lords of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beaujeu">Beaujeu</a> and then the dukes of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ile-bourbon">Bourbon</a>. After the confiscation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-iii-duke-of-bourbon">Constable of Bourbon's</a> lands in 1523 it was held by the crown, then restored in 1560 to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon-montpensier">Bourbon-Montpensier</a> family, who ruled it as a sovereign principality outside the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-france">Kingdom of France</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The princes kept a parliament at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trevoux">Trévoux</a>, minted coin and taxed separately, though in practice the land was closely tied to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anne-marie-louise-dorleans-duchess-of-montpensier">Anne Marie Louise d'Orléans</a>, La Grande Mademoiselle, held it and in 1681 ceded it to the Duke of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-maine">Maine</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV's</a> legitimised son. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuits</a> at Trévoux published the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/journal-de-trevoux">Journal de Trévoux</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dictionnaire-de-trevoux">Dictionnaire de Trévoux</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1762 the Duke of Maine's son, the Count of Eu, exchanged the principality with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xv">Louis XV</a> for lands in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, and it became part of the kingdom.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="principality, 1523 CE – 1762 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">principality</p><p class="st-emblem-region">France and the Low Countries</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:90.01%;width:4.76%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1523 CE – 1762 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Trévoux</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Anne Marie Louise d'Orléans, Louis-Auguste, Duke of Maine, Louis-Charles, Count of Eu</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Dombes</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1642&amp;focus=principality-of-dombes" aria-label="Principality of Dombes on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4793 560 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Principality of Dombes lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5113 816L5054 728"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5113 816h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5113 816h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Trévoux. <a href="/atlas?year=1642&amp;focus=principality-of-dombes">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
